<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qufu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qufu is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, the capital of the State of Lu in the Zhou period and the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confucius">Confucius</a>. Its Temple of Confucius, the Kong family mansion and the Cemetery of Confucius form a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. The descendants of Confucius lived there for more than two thousand years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qufu.jpg" alt="Qufu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 호고호 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhou_Gong_Miao_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
